<% content_for(:title, "#{@label} — Focus Order") %>

<%# The studioBoard factory, rendered ONCE at page level. A <script> inside the
    board component template would be cloned and re-parsed by the component and
    never run — the engine's own note on _board_assets. It self-guards, so a
    layout that later adopts it does not double-define. %>
<%= render "studio/board_assets" %>

<style>
  /* THE RANK IS THE POSITION, so the number is a COUNTER over the list rather
     than a value any template writes. After a drop the cards have moved and the
     numbering is already correct — no re-render, no JS, and no second source of
     truth to drift from the order it is describing. */
  #dropzone-focus { counter-reset: focus-rank; }
  #dropzone-focus .kanban-card { counter-increment: focus-rank; }
  #dropzone-focus .kanban-card .tt-rank-badge::before { content: counter(focus-rank); }

  /* The engine's dropzone reserves most of the viewport height, which is right
     for a kanban row of columns and wrong for one list — a three-game week drew
     an acre of dashed border under it. Keep a floor generous enough to be an
     easy drop target and let the list size the rest. */
  @media (min-width: 640px) { #dropzone-focus { min-height: 12rem; } }
</style>

<div class="max-w-screen-md mx-auto py-8 px-4 space-y-6">
  <div class="min-w-0">
    <%= link_to "← All weeks", admin_nfl_weeks_path, class: "text-xs text-muted hover:text-heading" %>
    <h1 class="text-heading text-2xl font-bold mt-1 mb-1"><%= @label %></h1>
    <p class="text-muted text-sm max-w-2xl">
      Drag to set the order the live board prefers — the top game leads. Each
      drop saves on its own; there is nothing to submit. The list starts in
      kickoff order, which is exactly what the board does on its own, so an
      untouched week is already correct and dragging is how you disagree with it.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted text-sm max-w-2xl mt-2">
      The order is a TIEBREAK, not an override: the board first narrows the week
      to the games eligible right now — being played, or inside the twelve hours
      before the next kickoff — and the highest game in THAT set leads. So
      putting the night game first will not take the board off the afternoon
      games it is competing with.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%# WHAT THE ORDER DOES, on the page that sets it. Recomputed on each load
      from the same service /live calls, so this is the answer, not a mock-up of
      it. It is a page-load reading: it does not follow a drag until you reload. %>
  <div class="card p-4 flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap" data-test="week-focus-now">
    <span class="text-[10px] text-muted uppercase tracking-wide">Focus right now</span>
    <% if @focus_now %>
      <%# Full names, matching the cards below — the abbreviations are for a
          scoreboard read at a glance, and this line is read once. %>
      <span class="text-heading font-semibold">
        <%= @focus_now.away_team&.name || @focus_now.away_team_slug %>
        <span class="text-muted font-normal">at</span>
        <%= @focus_now.home_team&.name || @focus_now.home_team_slug %>
      </span>
      <% if @focus_now.focus_rank %>
        <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">#<%= @focus_now.focus_rank %> in the order</span>
      <% end %>
    <% else %>
      <span class="text-muted text-sm">No games in this week.</span>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <% if @games.empty? %>
    <div class="card p-8 text-center">
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">No games on file for this week.</p>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <%# The engine's board primitive, in its within-lane REORDER-ONLY shape:
        one column, `group: false` so nothing can be dragged out of it, and no
        move_url because there is nowhere to move to. A drop POSTs the whole
        list's new order to reorder_url. %>
    <%= render "studio/board/board",
          columns: [
            { key: Admin::Nfl::WeeksController::FOCUS_ZONE,
              label: "Focus order",
              cards: @games,
              count: @games.size }
          ],
          card_partial: "admin/nfl/weeks/game_card",
          card_as: :card,
          card_locals: { zone: Admin::Nfl::WeeksController::FOCUS_ZONE },
          reorder_url: reorder_admin_nfl_week_path(params[:id]),
          reorder_payload: :slugs,
          group: false,
          id_attr: "slug",
          zone_attr: "stage",
          empty_label: "No games this week" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
